From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:47:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] execute_code: cap the spill a remote file-RPC
 terminal() result inlines; document raw spill output

Follow-up to #1868 review 5886172435 (card t_01a1d332eeab779a).

- The file-RPC poller ships each result base64 through env.execute stdin
  (Modal's legacy server path caps a stdin buffer at 2 MB; Daytona/Vercel
  stage it as an upload). It now inlines at most 1 MiB of spill; a bigger
  one keeps the window with truncated: True and full_output_path. The local
  socket transport keeps the 20 MB cap.
- The execute_code terminal() doc line says a long output comes raw from
  the spill (redacted, no sudo notes or transform_terminal_output rewrites).
  Prompt-surface snapshot re-rendered.
- Nit 1 (truncated accuracy without a spill) already landed in 7813e50fa2.
